 ## 2026-07-21
 
+### 0245 — VPN lifecycle separates ownership, enablement, system state, and runtime capability (TASK-260715-1q4qhw)
+- DECISION: A manager is owned only when its protocol is `NETunnelProviderProtocol`, its provider bundle ID exactly matches the accepted platform binding, and its stable provider-configuration marker matches. Labels, server address, enabled state, profile UUID, schema version, and array order never establish ownership. Every write/remove rechecks a freshly loaded object; unmarked lookalikes and duplicates are zero-write conflicts outside explicit inactive duplicate repair.
+- PLATFORM FINDING: Apple limits `loadAllFromPreferences` to configurations created by the calling app, but enabling an enterprise VPN can cause the OS to disable another app's enterprise VPN. Therefore ordinary ensure preserves/creates a disabled configuration and explicit foreground user intent owns enable/save/reload. Relux never mutates the unrelated manager object and reports the system-level enable effect truthfully.
+- AUTHORITY: `NETunnelProviderSession.status` is the sole system-session authority; a fresh generation/sequence provider snapshot is the sole runtime capability authority. Host suspension/termination removes observers only. Provider start/stop once-gates and exact deadlines remain extension-owned and join the accepted coordinator cleanup.
+- RESIDUAL: Exact four-target bundle IDs, App Group, Keychain group, and entitlements are not yet accepted (`TASK-260715-ypo7yo`). Shared implementation proceeds through injected identities, while production composition fails closed instead of inventing values. Human ratification stays decoupled in `TASK-260717-1dsqnj`.
+
 ### 0211 — Coordinator fault suite freezes ownership boundaries and resource baselines (TASK-260715-32virr)
 - DECISION: Fault injection uses the coordinator's injected cancellation-check seam to fail at fourteen exact before/after ownership boundaries. This keeps production code unchanged while proving reverse rollback, one disconnecting publication, one terminal publication, exact error mapping, and single cleanup for configuration, SSH, TCP, DNS, packet plane, settings, and packet-read ownership.
 - COVERAGE: The explicit control table covers rejected duplicate starts, idempotent stops, healthy/stale/late callbacks in usable, stopping, disconnected, and failed states; phase gates now include configuration as well as SSH, TCP, DNS, packet preparation, settings apply, packet activation, and final health. All four mandatory dependency failures must revoke capability before cleanup begins.

