TASK-260715-1rsqrh,task,implement-session-control-and-status-projection,Implement VPN session control and truthful status projection,backlog,STORY-260715-eto58m,,"Implement the host controller from TASK-260715-1q4qhw. Start and stop only the freshly reloaded owned NETunnelProviderSession, observe system status as authority, request fresh read-only provider snapshots for capability authority, and reconcile after app relaunch without owning forwarding.","In scope: current-status preflight; bounded v1 start request matching stored configuration; synchronous start errors; 60-second connect observation; cancel-start stop; 15-second disconnect observation; initial status read plus exact-session notifications; 3-second read-only message and last-disconnect-error requests; exact public connection-error/provider-error/nil-error mapping; protocol negotiation; generation/sequence freshness; controller retirement and host relaunch. Out of scope: final UI wording, automatic reconnect, mutating provider RPC, profile switching UX, UDP implementation, analytics, manager persistence, and app-owned runtime state.","1. Start requires a fresh exact-owned current enabled manager and maps every NEVPNStatus preflight/terminal row and last-disconnect result without duplicate system calls; cancellation/60-second timeout stops and never claims connected. 2. Stop is idempotent, joins connecting/connected/reasserting/disconnecting work, observes terminal status for 15 seconds, and never claims cleanup on timeout. 3. Projection preserves NETunnelProviderSession as system-state authority and current provider snapshots as capability authority; every non-connected status clears capability and missing/stale/unsupported/out-of-order facts never synthesize it. 4. Read-only v1 messages enforce 3-second timeout, request correlation, size/version/schema/generation ordering, and controller-generation retirement. 5. Tests cover every status, all public NEVPNConnectionError values, provider/unknown/nil errors, fetch timeout/cancellation, app recreation, observer/task release, start/stop races, nil/late provider responses, and fresh recovery from system plus provider state.","[""TASK-260715-1q4qhw"",""TASK-260715-15vkvz"",""TASK-260715-lovbdz""]","[""TASK-260715-3lab1f"",""TASK-260715-bf3a2d"",""TASK-260715-2a1cp7"",""TASK-260715-3btpxm""]","[{""text"":""Implement session commands and combined state projection without app-owned forwarding state"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Run race stale-snapshot relaunch and version-compatibility tests"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Attach task-scoped state mapping and verification evidence"",""done"":false}]",,2026-07-15T01:16:19Z,2026-07-15T02:46:54Z,true,[],[],[]
TASK-260715-2hiabd,task,implement-ios-packet-tunnel-provider-adapter,Implement the thin iOS packet-tunnel provider adapter,backlog,STORY-260715-eto58m,,Implement the iOS NEPacketTunnelProvider target adapter that translates Apple lifecycle calls and packetFlow access into the shared production factories and TunnelRuntimeCoordinator. Keep policy and data-plane state in ReluxTunnelCore and use only public APIs.,"In scope: startTunnel options decoding, provider configuration reference loading, packetFlow adapter injection, network-settings application closure, app-message delegation, stop reason handling, provider error termination, system sleep callbacks where required for safe no-op behavior, privacy-safe logging, and iOS build settings already established by M0. Out of scope: duplicate packet or SSH state machines, UI code, private utun access, path reconnect, UDP relay, entitlements changes, and TestFlight packaging.","1. The adapter contains only platform translation and composition and has no independent packet, SSH, TCP, DNS, or route state machine. 2. startTunnel completes only when the shared runtime reaches its M1 usable point or returns one mapped error exactly once. 3. stopTunnel cancels the active generation, waits for bounded cleanup, records the Apple stop reason, and calls its completion exactly once. 4. App messages are size-bounded and delegated to the shared versioned router even after the containing app has relaunched. 5. The iOS provider builds with approved public APIs and automated adapter tests cover duplicate start, stop during start, mapped failure, late callback, and deallocation.","[""TASK-260715-1q4qhw"",""TASK-260715-3ejhyy"",""TASK-260715-3tlgwm"",""TASK-260715-1bp6eu""]","[""TASK-260715-3lab1f""]","[{""text"":""Implement only the iOS platform translation and shared-runtime composition"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Run iOS provider build lifecycle and completion-handler tests"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Attach task-scoped adapter and public-API verification evidence"",""done"":false}]",,2026-07-15T01:16:19Z,2026-07-15T01:29:21Z,true,[],[],[]
TASK-260715-3dv8ea,task,implement-macos-packet-tunnel-provider-adapter,Implement the thin macOS packet-tunnel provider adapter,backlog,STORY-260715-eto58m,,"Implement the macOS NEPacketTunnelProvider target adapter that translates Apple lifecycle calls and packetFlow access into the same shared production factories and TunnelRuntimeCoordinator used on iOS, while preserving the generated product boundary from the legacy app.","In scope: startTunnel options decoding, provider configuration reference loading, packetFlow injection, network-settings closure, app-message delegation, stop reason handling, provider error termination, sleep or wake callback safe handling where exposed, privacy-safe logging, and generated macOS target integration from M0. Out of scope: duplicate runtime logic, legacy SwiftPM product changes, system extension redesign, reconnect, UDP relay, Developer ID release, notarization, and app UI.","1. The macOS adapter is behaviorally conformant with the iOS adapter through shared tests and contains no duplicate packet, SSH, TCP, DNS, or route policy. 2. Start and stop completion handlers fire once at the same shared-runtime readiness and cleanup boundaries as iOS. 3. Provider messages and stop reasons use the common versioned and privacy-safe contracts. 4. Host-app termination or relaunch does not tear down or recreate the active provider runtime. 5. The generated macOS host and provider build and adapter tests cover duplicate start, stop during start, mapped failure, late callback, and clean deallocation without touching the legacy release target.","[""TASK-260715-1q4qhw"",""TASK-260715-3ejhyy"",""TASK-260715-3tlgwm"",""TASK-260715-1bp6eu""]","[""TASK-260715-3lab1f""]","[{""text"":""Implement the macOS adapter through the same shared lifecycle contract"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Run generated macOS build conformance and cleanup tests"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Attach task-scoped adapter and legacy-isolation evidence"",""done"":false}]",,2026-07-15T01:16:19Z,2026-07-15T01:29:21Z,true,[],[],[]
TASK-260715-3lab1f,task,add-vpn-manager-and-provider-lifecycle-tests,Add VPN manager and provider lifecycle automation,backlog,STORY-260715-eto58m,,"Build automated host and provider test suites that exercise owned-manager persistence, session control, status projection, versioned app messaging, both platform adapters, stop cleanup, and containing-app recreation using protocol seams and generated-target integration tests.","In scope: unrelated manager fixtures, save or reload conflicts, permission and invalid states, connect and disconnect races, provider start failures, app-message versions, app recreation, stop reasons, completion once, repeated lifecycle loops, and resource baselines. Out of scope: physical system permission dialogs, final UI tests, packet throughput, DNS leak capture, reconnect, UDP, TestFlight, and notarization.","1. Manager tests prove idempotent single-owned configuration and preservation of unrelated configurations under success, conflict, and corruption cases. 2. Session tests cover every Network Extension status plus out-of-order notification and snapshot combinations. 3. Shared provider conformance tests run for iOS and macOS adapters and cover cancellation at each startup step, duplicate calls, messages, errors, and cleanup. 4. At least one hundred simulated start, host recreation, message, and stop cycles show no monotonic task, observer, descriptor, manager, or runtime growth. 5. Generated host and provider integration tests compile and run with deterministic fixtures and publish commands and expected results.","[""TASK-260715-15vkvz"",""TASK-260715-1rsqrh"",""TASK-260715-2hiabd"",""TASK-260715-3dv8ea"",""TASK-260715-1bp6eu""]","[""TASK-260715-3f4rhy"",""TASK-260715-13gzxe"",""TASK-260715-12x6oq"",""TASK-260715-1fpr3u"",""TASK-260715-132kb2""]","[{""text"":""Cover manager session messaging and both provider adapters in automation"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Run repeated lifecycle and resource-baseline suites"",""done"":false},{""text