    56	## 3. Exact manager ownership and canonical configuration
    57	
    58	### 3.1 Stable constants
    59	
    60	```text
    61	ownerKey                 = "works.relux.tunnel.owner"
    62	ownerValue               = "relux-tunnel"
    63	managerContractKey       = "works.relux.tunnel.manager-contract-version"
    64	managerContractVersion   = 1  (NSNumber/Int, not String)
    65	configurationReferenceKey= "works.relux.tunnel.configuration-reference"
    66	serverAddressSentinel    = "relux.invalid"
    67	startRequestKey          = "works.relux.tunnel.start-request"
    68	```
    69	
    70	`relux.invalid` is a technical non-routable sentinel, not an SSH endpoint and
    71	not final product copy. `localizedDescription` is injected localized display
    72	text and is never an identity field.
    73	
    74	### 3.2 Owned-manager predicate
    75	
    76	For the current platform, `isOwned(manager)` is true if and only if all of:
    77	
    78	1. `manager.protocolConfiguration` is an `NETunnelProviderProtocol`;
    79	2. `protocol.providerBundleIdentifier == platform.providerBundleID` using
    80	   exact, case-sensitive equality;
    81	3. `protocol.providerConfiguration?[ownerKey]` is a `String` exactly equal to
    82	   `ownerValue`.
    83	
    84	No other field participates. In particular, localized description,
    85	`serverAddress`, enabled state, profile UUID, manager-contract version, array
    86	position, and current session status do not establish ownership. A manager
    87	whose bundle ID matches but whose marker is absent or malformed is a
    88	`legacyOrForeignCandidate`: it is never edited, disabled, or removed by v1.
    89	
    90	The proof obligation is mechanical: every mutation/removal entry point MUST
    91	accept only an object returned by a fresh `loadAllFromPreferences` call and
    92	MUST re-evaluate `isOwned` immediately before the mutation. Tests provide mixed
    93	manager arrays covering other providers, other protocol classes, lookalike
    94	labels, missing/wrong/type-confused markers, and future schema versions; mocks
    95	must record zero setter/save/remove calls for every false row.
    96	
    97	### 3.3 Canonical v1 fields
    98	
    99	An owned current manager has:
   100	
   101	- a newly constructed `NETunnelProviderProtocol` (never merge arbitrary keys);
   102	- `providerBundleIdentifier = platform.providerBundleID`;
   103	- `serverAddress = "relux.invalid"`;
   104	- `disconnectOnSleep = false`;
   105	- `includeAllNetworks = false`, `excludeLocalNetworks = false`, and
   106	  `enforceRoutes = false`; reconnect/fail-closed policy remains reserved;
   107	- `providerConfiguration` containing exactly `ownerKey`,
   108	  `managerContractKey`, and `configurationReferenceKey`;
   109	- `configurationReferenceKey` as `Data` produced by
   110	  `RuntimeConfigurationCodec.encode(TunnelConfigurationReference)` and bounded
   111	  to 4 KiB; it contains schema v1 and one opaque profile UUID only;
   112	- `onDemandEnabled = false`, no On Demand rules, no app rules;
   113	- caller-provided localized description; and
   114	- no username/password, private key, passphrase, host-key bytes, raw profile,
   115	  destination, packet, log, or diagnostic payload.
   116	
   117	The owner marker determines ownership across supported schema upgrades. The
   118	manager contract and reference schema determine whether an owned manager is
   119	current. Version `> 1` yields `updateRequired` and MUST NOT be downgraded.
   120	Version `< 1`, wrong types, missing reference, invalid UUID, or codec failure
   121	yields `ownedConfigurationCorrupt`; repair requires an explicit current desired
   122	profile and replaces the complete protocol object. Without that input, no
   123	write occurs.
   124	
   125	## 4. Repository operations and persistence outcomes
   126	
   127	All repository calls are serialized per process. Each Apple preference call
   128	has a 15-second local deadline. NetworkExtension completion callbacks cannot
   129	be cancelled; cancellation/timeout retires the local operation token, ignores
   130	its late callback, marks cache state unknown, and forces a fresh load before
   131	the next action.
   132	
   133	### 4.1 Discover/ensure
   134	
   135	1. Call `NETunnelProviderManager.loadAllFromPreferences`.
   136	2. On load error, return a stable mapped error; create nothing. A nil managers
   137	   collection is also failure even when Apple supplies nil error:
   138	   `preferencesLoadReturnedNoCollection`. Only a non-nil successful collection
   139	   may be partitioned; nil never means zero configurations and permits no
   140	   create/save/remove.
   141	3. Partition with the exact predicate without mutating any manager.
   142	4. Zero owned and no legacy/foreign candidate: create a new disabled manager,
   143	   assign the canonical protocol, and save.
   144	5. One owned: validate; when desired fields differ, replace the complete
   145	   protocol object while preserving its current enabled state, then save.
   146	6. More than one owned: return `duplicateOwnedManagers(count)` with no writes.
   147	   Normal ensure never chooses by array order and never silently deletes.
   148	7. Any bundle-ID lookalike lacking the marker: return
   149	   `legacyOrForeignCandidate` instead of creating a second lookalike.
   150	8. After every successful save, discard the instance, load all again, require
   151	   exactly one matching owned manager, validate the persisted fields, and
   152	   return that reloaded object only. Save success without reload success is
   153	   `savedButReloadFailed`; callers must not start from the stale object.
   154	
   155	Repeated create/update with zero or one owned manager is idempotent. Duplicate
   156	repair is a distinct explicit operation. First decode every exact-owned
   157	manager's manager-contract and configuration-reference schema without mutation.
   158	If any is newer than supported or cannot be proven current/explicitly repairable,
   159	return `futureOwnedConfigurationConflict` / `updateRequired(version)` and make
   160	no change; future-owned data is never removed or downgraded. Otherwise, only
   161	while every supported exact-owned session is `.disconnected` or `.invalid`,
   162	remove the freshly revalidated supported duplicates, reload to prove zero, then
   163	call ensure to create one. If any is connecting, connected, reasserting, or
   164	disconnecting, return `duplicateOwnedManagersActive` and make no change. Every
   165	removal rechecks ownership, supported schema, and terminal session state against
   166	the fresh load.
   167	
   168	### 4.2 Enable/disable and permission
   169	
   170	Ensure never changes disabled to enabled. `enableOwnedManager` requires
   171	explicit foreground user intent (and the separate disclosure gate when added),
   172	fresh discovery, exactly one current owned manager, and no active transition.
   173	It sets `isEnabled = true`, saves, reloads, and succeeds only if the reloaded
   174	manager is still owned/current/enabled.
   175	
   176	This separation is required because Apple documents that enabling an
   177	enterprise VPN configuration can disable another app's enterprise VPN. Relux
   178	does not call setters/save/remove on unrelated managers, but the OS may change
   179	which enterprise VPN is enabled. The host must present this as a system-level
   180	enable effect, not claim that unrelated configurations are preserved enabled.
   181	
   182	Disable is also explicit, fresh-loads and rechecks ownership, requests session
   183	stop first, waits up to 15 seconds for `.disconnected`/`.invalid`, then sets
   184	`isEnabled = false`, saves, reloads, and verifies. On timeout it does not save.
   185	
   186	There is no preflight permission boolean. The first valid save/enable is the
   187	permission/authorization operation. iOS and macOS use framework-managed public
   188	NetworkExtension behavior; v1 does not manufacture or persist an
   189	`AuthorizationRef`. Success is known only after save and reload. A non-NEVPN
   190	authorization/cancellation error maps to `authorizationFailed(platformDomain,
   191	platformCode)` rather than falsely asserting a public `permissionDenied` code.
   192	
   193	### 4.3 Remove
   194	
   195	Removal occurs only for explicit delete/uninstall/reset intent. It fresh-loads,
   196	requires exactly one exact-owned manager, stops an active session and observes
   197	terminal status, rechecks ownership, calls `removeFromPreferences`, then reloads
   198	and succeeds only when no exact-owned manager remains. Stop timeout, ownership
   199	change, duplicate conflict, or remove/reload error leaves the configuration in
   200	place. No bulk “remove all VPN” operation exists.
   201	
   202	### 4.4 Stale configuration
   203	
   204	On `NEVPNError.configurationStale`, retire the object, reload, recompute
   205	ownership, rebuild the intended mutation from immutable desired input, and
   206	retry save once. A second stale result becomes `concurrentModification`; no
   207	loop and no mutation of the old instance. `NEVPNConfigurationChange` invalidates
   208	the cache and triggers debounced rediscovery, never an automatic write.
   209	
   210	## 5. Host session control
   211	
   212	The controller retains observers/tasks only while its host-side instance is
   213	alive. Destroying the controller or containing app cancels app waits and removes
   214	observers; it never calls `stopTunnel` from deinit/termination/backgrounding.
   215	
   216	### 5.1 Start
   217	
   218	Start requires a freshly reloaded, exact-owned, current, enabled manager and a
   219	`NETunnelProviderSession` connection. The controller reads current status first:
